# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CoreAsia Gateway — Caddy reverse proxy + automatic HTTPS.
# Public host: api.coreasia.id  →  internal gateway:8081 (Fiber, APP_PORT=8081).
#
# ── TLS behind Cloudflare: pick ONE option ──────────────────────────────────
#
# OPTION A — DNS-only (grey cloud) + Caddy's automatic Let's Encrypt (simplest).
#   In Cloudflare DNS, set the A record `api` to "DNS only" (grey cloud).
#   Caddy completes the HTTP-01/TLS-ALPN challenge directly on ports 80/443 and
#   manages the cert automatically. No extra config needed below.
#   Trade-off: the origin IP is exposed (no Cloudflare proxy / WAF / caching).
#
# OPTION B — Proxied (orange cloud) + Cloudflare Origin Certificate.
#   Keep the A record proxied. Caddy CANNOT use Let's Encrypt through the proxy,
#   so issue a Cloudflare Origin Certificate (Cloudflare dashboard → SSL/TLS →
#   Origin Server → Create Certificate), copy the cert + key onto the VPS, mount
#   them into the caddy container, and replace the block below with:
#
#       api.coreasia.id {
#           tls /etc/caddy/origin-cert.pem /etc/caddy/origin-key.pem
#           encode gzip
#           reverse_proxy gateway:8081
#       }
#
#   Then set Cloudflare SSL/TLS mode to "Full (strict)". This hides the origin IP
#   and adds Cloudflare's WAF/CDN in front. Recommended for a gray-area product.
#
# Default below uses OPTION A. Switch to B if you keep the orange cloud on.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

api.coreasia.id {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy gateway:8081
}
